      "anchor": "global-short-isotropic-flag",
      "title": "The least size and the finite list of canonical jumps below one half",
      "equations": [],
      "dependencies": [],
      "hypotheses": "Positive rank self-dual Hermitian lattice over a CM field at an automorphic point, with the positive majorant frames. Use the size and saturation properties of its Harder–Narasimhan filtration.",
      "statement": "A nonzero step occurs at its largest quotient size. Its open and closed steps differ at a jump, and rank rises strictly there. The jumps below 1/2 form a finite increasing flag from zero to the strict half step. If the least size is below 1/2 it is the first jump.",
